 R←Test_005(debugFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;ns;assets;before;new;lines;file
⍝ Exercise `Notify` with an empty question, which is what `Select` passes when it has no
⍝ caption: the body must then name the type that is waiting.
⍝ The assets folder used here holds no `toast.ps1`, so nothing pops up and the file `Notify`
⍝ wrote is still there to be inspected.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 :If 'Win'≢3↑⊃# ⎕WG'APLVersion'
     R←T._WindowsOnly ⋄ →0
 :EndIf

 new←⍬
 assets←2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'TEMP'
 ns←⎕NS''
 {}ns.⎕FX ##.WindowsToast.⎕NR'Notify'
 {}'TatinVars'ns.⎕NS''
 {}ns.TatinVars.⎕FX(' r←GetFullPath2AssetsFolder')(' r←''',assets,'''')

 before←⊃0 1 ⎕NINFO⍠1⊢assets,'/dyalog-notify-*.txt'
 {}ns.Notify'Select' ''
 new←(⊃0 1 ⎕NINFO⍠1⊢assets,'/dyalog-notify-*.txt')~before
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1≠≢new
 lines←⊃⎕NGET(⊃new)1
 →T.GoToTidyUp 3≠≢lines
 →T.GoToTidyUp'Select is waiting for your input'≢2⊃lines

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 :For file :In new                              ⍝ `⎕NDELETE` is shy, so no `{}` here
     ⎕NDELETE file
 :EndFor
⍝Done
